<topic id="extension">
  <title>DITA Bootstrap Extension</title>

  <shortdesc>A plug-in for
    <xref href="http://www.dita-ot.org" format="html" scope="external">DITA Open Toolkit</xref> that extends the
    <xref href="https://infotexture.github.io/dita-bootstrap/" format="html" scope="external">DITA Bootstrap</xref> HTML
    output with additional features from the
    <xref
      href="https://bootstrapextensions.com"
      format="html"
      scope="external"
    >Bootstrap Extension</xref> library.</shortdesc>
  <body outputclass="language-markup">
    <section>
      <title>Installing</title>
      <p>Use the <cmdname>dita</cmdname> command to add the plug-ins to your DITA Open Toolkit installation:</p>
    </section>
     <accordion>
        <accordion-item open="yes">
        <title>DITA-OT 3.5 and newer</title>
          <ol>  
            <li>
              <p><b>Optional:</b> install the specialization plug-ins to add support for new DITA elements that
               generate Bootstrap Extension components:
              </p>
              <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >install</parmname> org.dita-bootstrap.specialization
<cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname>install</parmname> org.dita-bootstrap.specialization.extension</codeblock>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p>For HTML generation, install the CSS plug-in and the HTML plug-in as shown:
              </p>
              <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >install</parmname> fox.jason.extend.css
<cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname>install</parmname> org.dita-bootstrap.html
<cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname>install</parmname> org.dita-bootstrap.extension</codeblock>
            </li>
            <!-- li>
              <p>For PDF generation, install the PDF plug-in, and then <b
              >optionally</b> add the PDF theme plug-in as shown:
              </p>
              <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >install</parmname> org.dita-bootstrap.pdf
<cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname>install</parmname> org.dita-bootstrap.pdf.theme</codeblock>
            </li-->
            <li>
              <p>To add syntax highlighting using the Bootstrap color scheme, install the Prism.js plug-in if required:
              </p>
              <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >install</parmname> fox.jason.prismjs</codeblock>
            </li>
          </ol>
      </accordion-item>
      <accordion-item>
        <title>DITA-OT 3.3 and newer</title>
          <ol>  
            <li>
              <p><b>Optional:</b> install the specialization plug-in to add support for new DITA elements that
               generate Bootstrap components:
              </p>
              <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >--install</parmname> org.dita-bootstrap.specialization
<cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname>--install</parmname> org.dita-bootstrap.extension.specialization</codeblock>
          </li>
          <li>
          <p>For HTML generation, install the CSS plug-in and the HTML plug-in as shown:
          </p>
          <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >--install</parmname> fox.jason.extend.css
<cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname>--install</parmname> org.dita-bootstrap.html
<cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname>--install</parmname> org.dita-bootstrap.extension</codeblock>
          </li>
          <!--li>
          <p>For PDF generation, install the PDF plug-in, and then <b>optionally</b> add the PDF theme plug-in as shown:
          </p>
          <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >-/-install</parmname> org.dita-bootstrap.pdf
<cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname>-/-install</parmname> org.dita-bootstrap.pdf.theme</codeblock>
            </li-->
            <li>
              <p>To add syntax highlighting using the bootstrap color scheme, install the Prism.js plug-in if required:
              </p>
              <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >--install</parmname> fox.jason.prismjs</codeblock>
            </li>
          </ol>
      </accordion-item>
      <accordion-item>
        <title>DITA-OT 3.2 and older</title>
          <ol>  
            <li>
              <p><b>Optional:</b> install the specialization plug-in to add support for new DITA elements that
               generate Bootstrap components:
              </p>
              <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >--install</parmname> https://github.com/dita-bootstrap/dita-bootstrap.specialization/archive/master.zip
<cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >--install</parmname> https://github.com/dita-bootstrap/dita-bootstrap.extension.specialization/archive/master.zip</codeblock>
            </li>
            <li>
              <p>For HTML generation, install the CSS plug-in and the HTML plug-in as shown:
              </p>
              <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >--install</parmname> https://github.com/jason-fox/fox.jason.extend.css/archive/master.zip
<cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >--install</parmname> https://github.com/dita-bootstrap/dita-bootstrap.html/archive/master.zip
<cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >--install</parmname> https://github.com/dita-bootstrap/dita-bootstrap.extension/archive/master.zip</codeblock>
            </li>
            <!--li>
              <p>For PDF generation, install the PDF plug-in, and then <b
              >optionally</b> add the PDF theme plug-in as shown:
              </p>
              <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >-/-install</parmname> https://github.com/dita-bootstrap/dita-bootstrap.pdf/archive/master.zip
<cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >-/-install</parmname> https://github.com/dita-bootstrap/dita-bootstrap.pdf.theme/archive/master.zip</codeblock>
            </li-->
            <li>
              <p>To add syntax highlighting using the bootstrap color scheme, install the Prism.js plug-in if required:
              </p>
              <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
              >--install</parmname> https://github.com/jason-fox/fox.jason.prismjs/archive/master.zip</codeblock>
            </li>
          </ol>   
      </accordion-item>
    </accordion>
    <section>
      <title>Using</title>
      <p>If using DITA specialization for the Bootstrap Extension, ensure that the <codeph
        >*.dita</codeph> files are using the following <codeph>DOCTYPE</codeph> declaration:</p>
        <codeblock
        outputclass="language-xml"
      >&lt;!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC "-//Infotexture//DTD DITA Bootstrap Extension Topic//EN" "bootstrap-ext-topic.dtd"&gt;</codeblock>
      <p>Specify the <option>html5-bootstrap</option> format when building output with the <cmdname>dita</cmdname>
        command:</p>
      <codeblock outputclass="language-bash"><cmdname>dita</cmdname> <parmname
        >--input</parmname>=path/to/your.ditamap <parmname>--format</parmname>=html5-bootstrap</codeblock>
    </section>
    <section>
      <title outputclass="h3">Optional elements</title>
      <p>The optional <codeph>toTop</codeph> button can be included with the following parameter:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <parmname>to-top.include</parmname> – add a
          <xref href="./to-top.dita" format="dita">toTop button</xref> that scrolls to the top of the page
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section>
      <title outputclass="h3">Common Bootstrap utility classes</title>
      <p>The HTML output can be annotated with common Bootstrap utility classes using additional command line
        parameters:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <parmname>bootstrap.css.to-top</parmname> – common Bootstrap utility classes for the
          <xref href="./to-top.dita" format="dita">toTop button</xref>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section>
      <note type="note">Within the sample documentation, the texts describing the usage of each component have been
        copied directly from the
        <xref href="https://bootstrapextensions.com/" format="html" scope="external">official Bootstrap Extension
          documentation</xref>, however DITA markup is used throughout the examples describing how to implement these
        components correctly using the DITA <xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt> attribute. This text is therefore a derivative
        of <cite>Bootstrap Extension</cite> AKK IT, Inc, and used under
        <xref href="https://opensource.org/license/MIT/" format="html" scope="external">MIT</xref>.</note>
    </section>
  </body>
</topic>
